# PR #540 — force LF line endings for shell scripts so Docker builds
# don't hit the bash "pipefail: invalid option name" trap on line 2
# of a script that Windows-native git checked out with CRLF. Applies
# to any *.sh across the repo (backend/scripts/, native/zebrash-cli/,
# etc.) — none of them should ever ship with \r\n.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same story for Go source and Makefiles — LF everywhere to keep
# Linux/macOS runners happy regardless of who committed from what OS.
*.go text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
